{
  "result": "If I could flip just one switch, I wouldn't try to make everyone agree, or always happy, or end every conflict overnight.\n\nI'd make sure no one falls below a basic floor.\n\nNo one goes to sleep hungry. No one dies from a treatable illness or lack of clean water. No one is homeless in the cold, or denied an education because they were born in the wrong place.\n\nNot because that would create a perfect world \u2014 people would still argue, disagree, face hard choices, and grieve. But it would remove the most unnecessary kind of suffering.\n\nAnd the frustrating thing is, we already have the food, the medicine, the knowledge, and the technology to do it. It's mostly a coordination and caring problem. If that floor was guaranteed, everything else changes downstream: kids can actually learn, people aren't desperate enough to turn to violence to survive, communities can plan for the future instead of just getting through today.\n\nIt feels like the one change that would let humanity actually argue about the *interesting* problems, instead of the preventable ones.\n\nWhat about you \u2014 if you had that one switch, what would you pull?",
